From: Koral Ilgun <koral.ilgun@adtran.com> 
Date: Fri Aug 14 16:24:37 2026 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: do not log an adopted interface clash as an error

nl80211_create_iface() is called with use_existing=1 during radio
reconfiguration. The kernel returns ENFILE from NL80211_CMD_NEW_INTERFACE
when a netdev of that name already exists, and the caller then adopts it
("Continue using existing interface"). The failure is expected on that
path, but it was logged at error level, so every boot produced several
"Failed to create interface wifiXg: -23 (Too many open files in system)"
lines that look like fd exhaustion.

Pass use_existing down and log the clash at debug level when the netdev
exists. A real create failure, and the retry after the interface is
removed, still log at error level.

Signed-off-by: Koral Ilgun <koral.ilgun@adtran.com>
---
 src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c |   14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -6855,7 +6855,7 @@ static int nl80211_create_iface_once(str
 				     enum nl80211_iftype iftype,
 				     const u8 *addr, int wds, u32 radio_mask,
 				     int (*handler)(struct nl_msg *, void *),
-				     void *arg)
+				     void *arg, int use_existing)
 {
 	struct nl_msg *msg;
 	int ifidx;
@@ -6931,7 +6931,12 @@ static int nl80211_create_iface_once(str
 	if (ret) {
 	fail:
 		nlmsg_free(msg);
-		wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR, "Failed to create interface %s: %d (%s)",
+		/* With use_existing the caller adopts the existing netdev, so a
+		 * name clash here is expected and handled in
+		 * nl80211_create_iface(). Do not report it as an error. */
+		wpa_printf((use_existing && if_nametoindex(ifname)) ?
+			   MSG_DEBUG : MSG_ERROR,
+			   "Failed to create interface %s: %d (%s)",
 			   ifname, ret, strerror(-ret));
 		return ret;
 	}
@@ -6998,7 +7003,7 @@ int nl80211_create_iface(struct wpa_driv
 		return nl80211_use_existing_iface(drv, ifname, iftype, addr);
 
 	ret = nl80211_create_iface_once(drv, ifname, iftype, addr, wds, radio_mask,
-					handler, arg);
+					handler, arg, use_existing);
 
 	/* if error occurred and interface exists already */
 	if (ret < 0 && if_nametoindex(ifname)) {
@@ -7013,7 +7018,8 @@ int nl80211_create_iface(struct wpa_driv
 
 		/* Try to create the interface again */
 		ret = nl80211_create_iface_once(drv, ifname, iftype, addr,
-						wds, radio_mask, handler, arg);
+						wds, radio_mask, handler, arg,
+						0);
 	}
 
 	if (ret >= 0 && is_p2p_net_interface(iftype)) {
